      },
      "text": "Friday – Full-day tour to Angel Falls"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6197a092a5efb4ddf3babeacf50dd831a15edd03d7cd177d634c2149a0867049",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-0a822c5ae0173752",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Set out early in motorised curiaras, traditional boats that take you up the Carrao River through Mayupa Lagoon and the Arautaima rapids.\n\nHave breakfast at a camp overlooking the Auyán-tepui massif. Then continue to Devil’s Canyon.\n\nOn reaching Ratóncito Island, set out on foot through the forest. After about an hour, you’ll reach a lookout overlooking Angel Falls, the highlight of the day. The water plunges from a height of almost a kilometre.\n\nAfter seeing the falls, start the return journey. Local guides may offer a chance to swim in the pool at the foot of the falls. Then enjoy a traditional Indigenous lunch, return to Canaima Lagoon for dinner and stay overnight at the hotel.\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast, lunch and dinner.\n\n**Important:** This is an active full-day tour involving a motorboat ride, a crossing and a short hike. Bring comfortable trainers or hiking shoes, a change of comfortable clothes and a rain jacket."
    },
